      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Momentum has finally tilted Toronto's way - and it's about time. <strong>The Blue Jays' 5-1 win over the Cardinals last night</strong> gave them a third straight victory, a clean edge after a rough summer and a reminder that the bats can still bite when the club strings together innings. At 52-59, fifth in the AL East and 13.5 games back, this is no pennant drive; it is a late-summer salvage job. Still, the recent run - 5-2 over the Nationals, then 3-1 and 5-1 against St. Louis - has brought some dignity back to the room. Kevin Gausman's standing ovation in what could be a Toronto farewell hangs over the club like a storm cloud and a tribute at once. <strong>Now comes another Cardinals test Sunday afternoon at 1:37, and Toronto has a chance to keep the grind alive</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated August 2, 2026"
      },
