        "body": "The silence is the story now - and in Toronto, that usually means a hard decision is coming. <strong>The biggest pulse in camp is the Kawhi Leonard hold-up, with the Clippers' investigation still hanging over any move</strong>, while the Raptors wait for clarity instead of forcing the issue. They sit in the deep offseason, 42-32 and 3rd in the Atlantic Division, with the roster already being massaged around the edges: Kyle Anderson is in, Chris Paul is out, and Markelle Fultz got a 10-day look. The club has also set its 2026 training camp and preseason schedule, the first real checkpoint on the calendar. Scottie Barnes remains the cornerstone, but the question is whether Toronto is done tinkering or still hunting a bigger swing. <strong>Training camp will tell us whether this is a neat retool or the start of something far more ambitious</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated August 2, 2026"
