      "title": "Sunday's Skate",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Blue Jays are back at it this afternoon after a 5-1 win over the Cardinals, with Kevin Gausman drawing attention after a standing ovation in what Sportsnet called a potential Toronto farewell. They are 52-59 and fourth in the AL East, and first pitch against St. Louis is set for 1:37 p.m. ET on Sportsnet.",
        "For the Leafs, the focus is squarely on the future, with No. 1 pick Gavin McKenna and Sergei Bobrovsky highlighted as key pieces for 2026-27, while Nick Paul is being cast as the kind of Swiss-army knife who fits anywhere in the lineup. The Raptors are still in deep offseason mode too, with questions around Kawhi Leonard and a season opener against the Heat on Oct. 3.",
        "The Commanders are in training camp and being sized up through a different lens, with observers pointing to Styles, Chenal and Luvu as possible keys and a matchup at Philadelphia on Sept. 13 next on the calendar."
